But `updateGame(step, t)` uses t from clockLoop.elapsedTime, not sim time. Pose uses t for idle sin; it will be ~real time; fine. The fixed steps simulate 2 frames at a time if 60fps; t constant during those steps, but that's negligible. Better maintain `simT += step` each update and pass. Add global let simT=0; use simT. In updateGame, state.elapsed increments. Camera can use clockLoop.elapsedTime. Use t for visual only. Fine.
```
let simT=0;
while... { simT+=step; updateGame(step,simT); }
```
