content.text:
AwayShot counted 23 samples during the windup, but no block. Why? `contestBlock` doesn't block if already cooldown 0.62; the first press during windup should work. Unless pressing contest at the first windup tick: `w.t > w.dur*0.18`? The check runs immediately and fails early; then cooldown 0.62 means no more attempts during the 0.5s windup. Exactly. Our interval only triggers once at the start, gets cooldown, and no chance. In real play, the user presses at the apex. Need better block timing logic or shorter cooldown. Also user can hold space? `primaryDown` only on keydown (no repeat), so one attempt. This makes blocking nearly impossible. That's a gameplay bug relative to requirement "defensive controls" and blocks.

Fix contestBlock: make the contest cooldown 0.32 or allow block check to be latched: instead of a single check at press, set `d.contestTimer` and when the windup reaches its release, if a contest was active during the shot, block once. Better design:
- On press, set contestTimer=0.6, play animation, mark `d.blockAttempt = 0.6` and `state.blockWindow`?
- When `beginAwayShot` or `updateAwayWindup`, evaluate a block if any defender contested near at any point? That would be generous. In real play, contact/contest during the gather = block chance.
- Simpler: on press, if windup exists, allow repeated check during windup using a dedicated `state.blockTry` that lasts 0.45s and blocks if distance close, rather than immediate only.

Implement in contestBlock:
```
d.contestCd = 0.55;
d.contestTimer = 0.55;
setAnim...
state.blockAttempt = { defender: d, t: 0, dur: 0.55 };
```
Then in updateAwayWindup, each frame if state.blockAttempt and !w.blocked, check if w.t between 18% and 92%, defender within 1.9 and relative alignment maybe; if within, roll chance (or just roll once at start). We need a single roll per attempt. Add `state.blockAttempt.rolled`. At the first frame within window, roll; if success, block. This means pressing contest slightly early still can block at the right time (like a timed contest). User presses when rival starts shooting, works. And pressing after windup start also works if within duration.

But we also want skill: block only if contest pressed and defender in position. Chance 0.46 base. On failure, the shot continues with reduced chance due to contest.

Set `contestBlock` to also apply when no windup (just a contest animation). The block attempt lives 0.55s and applies to any windup starting within that window. That's fine.

If successful:
- `w.blocked = true; w.blockT = 0;` etc.
Then startLooseBall after 0.24. In updateAwayWindup, the block check currently in contestBlock. Move block logic to new function `updateBlockAttempt(dt)` called in updateGame before updateAwayWindup? Or integrate into contestBlock? I'll implement:
```
state.blockAttempt = { defender: d, t: 0, dur: 0.6, rolled: false };
```
In updateAwayWindup(dt):
```
const ba = state.blockAttempt;
if (ba && !w.blocked) {
  ba.t += dt;
  if (w.t > w.dur*0.12 && w.t < w.dur*0.9 && !ba.rolled) {
    ba.rolled = true;
    const dist = ...;
    if (dist < 1.85) {
      const chance = 0.5 + ...;
      if (Math.random()<chance) { block }
    }
  }
  if (ba.t>ba.dur) state.blockAttempt=null;
}
```
Also decrement in updateGame: `if (state.blockAttempt) { state.blockAttempt.t += dt; if (state.blockAttempt.t > dur) state.blockAttempt=null; }` but updateAwayWindup also. Put lifecycle in updateGame.

