What happened: `beginShot` sets shotType dunk; charge; at charge >0.73, goto away and release. But `releaseDunk` should increment attempts and set state.dunk. The screenshot at 0.8s still shows charging meter and ball above, suggesting `release()` didn't execute. Why? The interval might be clearing before the charge threshold because the tab throttled and screenshot state query happened at 0.8s with charging? Our state query only included poster/dunk/score/phase, not charging. The screenshot clearly shows charging (meter shown, TAKEOFF) and clock at 1:30. It may be that the 120ms setTimeout and interval are running in a throttled page, and the screenshot interrupted? Wait the page was reloaded, eval set timeouts; then we sleep 0.8 shell seconds; the page may be throttled to ~1fps, so by screenshot time only one frame. The timer at 1:30 means almost no game time advanced. The UI charge meter shows full because state.charge updated? It shows full green bar and ball at rim, maybe it's a dunk in progress but HUD attempts not updated? The scoreboard 0/0 means attempts 0. Hmm.

Actually the meter caption "DUNK" and "RIM RUN · DUNK", "TAKEOFF!", and the bar full yellow; it could be after release but HUD not updated? `releaseDunk` hides side meter (`hideSideMeter`) and sets shotType jumper, so meter should hide. Unless `releaseDunk` didn't run.

Wait, the screenshot shows the ball floating near the rim at y~260, Curry near free-throw line at z around -10? Not dunking yet. The meter is full, charging still true. So the interval hasn't fired. Charge is full (1.0) and still charging (bounces between 1 and down? updateGame sets chargeDir -1 at >=1, so it will decrease). Our threshold >0.73 should have fired long ago if the interval ran. The interval likely never ran because page timers are throttled? Or because `setInterval` started at 120ms and after reload? It should.

Maybe `c.state().charge` returns 0 in the interval because `state.charge` wasn't updating while page throttled? But screenshot shows full charge at 1:30. Hmm.

This test harness timing is unreliable due to headless throttling. Better add deterministic debug helpers to force a dunk directly. Add `__cs.dunkNow(poster)` that teleports and sets state.dunk with chosen params, without relying on charge. Useful for verifying animation/visual. But the real gameplay path is what matters; code looks correct. Still, visual verification of poster is useful. We can add a debug function that invokes `releaseDunk` after setting charge appropriate? Or call `beginShot` and then manually set `state.charge=0.8` then `releaseShot`. The current interval approach should work, but maybe charge returned stale because state() reads it; timing weird.

